# V3 (SOFT). IMAGE: tp4-stackfix-3 (built by V0b). THE TRIGGER UNDER THE EXACTNESS POLICY: the S2 G4 staggered plan (M10) on the base
# gate profile. Users arrive 30 s apart (c2_serving_gate.STAGGER_SECONDS) at S3a's lengths 4096 / 16384 / 32768 / 60000 (X2's, V2's),
# 4096 out (EOS on), so user 2's and user 3's prefills run AFTER padded two- and three-live packed rounds (replays of the attach-time block
# trace: v172's trigger), and every user's text is compared with its solo arm under the strict policy (one re-run on a first
# divergence), plus the padded-probe arm. V1a/V1b judge the trigger by text only and V2 never reaches it (the matrix admits all four
# users before round 1 and its solo arm serves one user at a time), so this is the one job that says the fix is EXACT, not coherent.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over the job file on a throwaway
# commit of tp4/stack-fix (or a descendant) and push the window tag. Nothing here names a rig, a card or a registry. THE DRIVER
# SUBSTITUTES C2_IMAGE_TAG FROM ITS IMAGE_TAG ENV: a chain that sets one IMAGE_TAG for all its jobs runs every job on that image.
# READ (c2-gate-summary.json, staggered-concurrent/server.log): list the users whose 'Prefilling 1 user(s)' line FOLLOWS a padded
# packed round ('[PINDIAG] packed padded round live=2' or 'live=3'; EOS is on, so an early answer can leave a later arrival alone:
# the trigger needs at least one such user, else the job did not exercise it). Each of them IDENTICAL to solo = the fix removes the
# mechanism; a divergence or garbage from their first token = it does not (this image already warms the eager prefill before the
# capture: read the '[PINDIAG] four-card prefill programs=' lines in server.log - a B-A-W above zero names an unwarmed shape,
# none names a victim outside the prefill set, so V5 next; ORDER.txt). SOFT because the plan has never run at four cards: its
# other S2 checks (the four-live rate above 13 tok/s net of the audits when four are live, idle commits, the probe) can fail for
# reasons that are not this defect; read each problem line before calling it.
# Duration (estimate): 35-60 min, the gate's worst case (a re-run of both judged arms) about 6 h.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset gate
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-stackfix-3
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-gate
C2_GATE_PLAN=staggered
C2_GATE_LENGTHS=4096,16384,32768,60000
C2_GATE_MAX_TOKENS=4096
C2_GATE_JIT=record
